*> Free-format source: no columns, comments start with *>.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. WORDS.

DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 SENTENCE   PIC X(60) VALUE "the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog".
01 WORD       PIC X(12).
01 PTR        PIC 99 VALUE 1.
01 N-WORDS    PIC 99 VALUE 0.
01 N-LONG     PIC 99 VALUE 0.
01 LONGEST    PIC X(12) VALUE SPACES.
01 WORD-LEN   PIC 99.
01 MAX-LEN    PIC 99 VALUE 0.
01 CAPITAL    PIC X(60).

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
main-para.
    PERFORM UNTIL PTR > FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(SENTENCE))
        MOVE SPACES TO WORD
        UNSTRING SENTENCE DELIMITED BY ALL SPACE
            INTO WORD
            WITH POINTER PTR
        END-UNSTRING
        ADD 1 TO N-WORDS
        COMPUTE WORD-LEN = FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WORD))
        IF WORD-LEN > 4 ADD 1 TO N-LONG END-IF
        IF WORD-LEN > MAX-LEN
            MOVE WORD-LEN TO MAX-LEN
            MOVE WORD TO LONGEST
        END-IF
    END-PERFORM
    DISPLAY N-WORDS " words, " N-LONG " longer than 4 letters"
    DISPLAY "longest word: " FUNCTION TRIM(LONGEST)
    MOVE FUNCTION UPPER-CASE(SENTENCE(1:1)) TO CAPITAL(1:1)
    MOVE SENTENCE(2:) TO CAPITAL(2:)
    DISPLAY FUNCTION TRIM(CAPITAL) "."
    STOP RUN.
